    "reason": "The release note [ev-e6c6c1eb424d] and the PR description [ev-9882d41028c7] only say \"update dependencies\", with no dependency names, versions or effects. The changed-files list [ev-e018a39f090c] shows that only e2e/go.mod, e2e/go.sum, go.mod and go.sum were touched. That points to an update of Go modules, but it does not say which modules changed or from which version to which. The evidence also says nothing about who is exposed or what happens if an operator does nothing. The \"BREAKING CHANGES\" heading covers the whole 36-item list, so it is not evidence about this item. To write the assertion we need the actual go.mod diff, meaning the module names and their old and new versions, or upstream text that describes the effect.",
